# The exceptions to the engine's rule against the console's terms (tools/engine_terms.zig, DESIGN.md
# P1, PLAN item 03): the legitimate cases only, such as a colour constant, or a chip's register in
# the sound's chip models. One entry a line:
#
#   PATH TERM -- WHY
#
# PATH is a file under src/shared, or a directory ending in `/`. TERM is the text as the source
# writes it (`0xFFFF`, `vblank_count`), or a class of terms: hex, vblank, register, vdp, vram, cram,
# vsram, cpu. WHY says why the term is not the console's place or name. An entry that allows
# nothing is an error.
